From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: winex11, explorer: a framed Linux program's menus stay open

David (2026-11-15): Steam's View, Friends, Games and Help menus appear "for
only a single frame and then disappear". Steam's menus are top-level X
windows of their own that close when they lose the X focus. Three things
took it from them, each a thing a window manager never does:

- The taskbar framed the menu. The compositor lists a transient window
  once its main window, framed (0762), is no longer a top-level it shows,
  and explorer put it in a Wine window of its own: reparented, it lost the
  focus and closed. Never framed now, and given no taskbar button: a window
  typed as a menu, tooltip, combo box list, drag icon or notification
  (_NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE), and an undecorated window (_MOTIF_WM_HINTS) that is
  transient for another (WM_TRANSIENT_FOR) or asks for no taskbar button
  (_NET_WM_STATE_SKIP_TASKBAR). SG_EMBED_QUERY says so (1 << 47); explorer
  remembers such windows while they are listed. Dialogs are framed as before.
- The click that opened the menu activates the frame afterwards (posted),
  and the frame gave the X focus back to the program's window. The focus is
  now asked for at the click's time -- the X server keeps a later focus, the
  menu's -- asked again at once should it have gone elsewhere (the
  compositor to Wine's desktop window), and never taken from the program's
  own menu (the same _NET_WM_PID, WM_TRANSIENT_FOR or WM_CLIENT_LEADER; a
  menu or an override-redirect popup).
- Framing a window that went meanwhile ended explorer, the shell: the
  error of a request with no reply (BadWindow on X_ChangeSaveSet) came after
  X11DRV_check_error had looked, to Xlib's fatal handler. Every check in
  sg_embed.c syncs first.

The compositor's side (it holds such a window hidden for 2.5 s as one the
taskbar will frame) is sg-compositor's, reported to the main session.

Gate: test/embedmenu-gate.sh (make test-embedmenu), with a stand-in program
(test/embedmenu-app.c) whose menus close on losing the focus: transient,
POPUP_MENU and override-redirect menus stay open, top-level, shown, with the
focus, no frame or button, also when the click is handled late; a window
not marked as a menu is still framed; the shell is still running after.
Mutants SG_MUTANT_EMBED_FRAMES_MENUS, SG_MUTANT_EMBED_FOCUS_OVER_MENU and
SG_MUTANT_EMBED_ERROR_UNSYNCED each fail it.
